/* js/data-raid.js — the Raid module: The Venomous Abyss
   Load order: data-shared → data-mplus → data-raid → render → app.
   All five load with `defer`, which preserves this order. */

/* ═══ RAID · THE VENOMOUS ABYSS ═════════════════════════════════════════════
   Eight bosses inside the Vaults of Atal'Utek, patch 12.1. Scope: Normal
   and Heroic. Mythic and LFR are deliberately out of scope for now — the
   difficulty model already accommodates them (df takes a third value), so
   adding either later is data, not structure.

   THE FORK. The raid is not linear: after Nek'zali it splits into two wings
   — Entombed Sentinels → Vashnik, and The Lost Explorers → Sszorak — which
   converge at the Twin Fangs. Sources list the middle four in different
   orders because each is describing one walk of the same graph; that is not
   a naming dispute and must not be filed as one. `o` is the canonical
   listing index used by the switcher; never render it as a kill-order claim
   for a fork boss — use `pos` instead.

   Ability shape mirrors DUNGEONS: {n,t,c,r,sev,e,h,s} plus:
     df : difficulties the ability exists on — ["h"] for Heroic-only.
          Absent means both. Never write ["n","h"] explicitly; absence is
          the both-difficulties spelling and the checker enforces it.
     hh : Heroic-only addendum to the tactic, rendered only on Heroic.
   Bosses carry phases:[{n,trigger,a:[...]}] — flat a:[] stays legal for a
   phaseless boss.

   Names are Wowhead's where Wowhead has them; the raid is new enough that
   many entities have no entry yet, so IV/Method agreement stands in until
   the database moves. wow.gg reads like a translation and disagrees on
   several names — those variants live in CORRECTIONS, not here. wow.gg also
   describes the MYTHIC versions of fights by its own admission, so it is
   cited for structure, loot and Ula'tek, not for Normal/Heroic specifics.
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
